The licence texts are in LICENSE-MIT and LICENSE-APACHE.

Tempo ported it to the GPUI that gpui-kit 0.7.1 bundles, replaced the PTY reader and writer with
channels, and added scrollback, mouse selection, clipboard, wheel and focus handling. Those changes
are under the same licences.

It uses alacritty_terminal 0.25.1 (Apache-2.0) for parsing and the grid. No code comes from Zed's
GPL-3.0 crates.
